        -:    8:/**
        -:    9: * @file stability.c
        -:   10: * @brief Hold-stability score — implementation.
        -:   11: *
        -:   12: * Per 50 Hz frame, three EMA-weighted RMS estimates drive the score:
        -:   13: *   - RMS_omega: |gyro|, single-pole EMA on the squared magnitude     (tremor)
        -:   14: *   - RMS_accel: bandpass(|a|), single-pole EMA on the squared mag    (sway)
        -:   15: *   - RMS_disp:  geodesic |q ⊖ qref|, single-pole EMA on the squared
        -:   16: *                angle, where qref is a slow EMA of the orientation   (drift)
        -:   17: *
        -:   18: * Each term is normalised to a per-archer baseline, combined with
        -:   19: * expert weights into an instability index I, and mapped to 0..100 by
        -:   20: * an exponential decay (score = 100*exp(-k*I): I=0 -> 100, I=1 -> 50).
        -:   21: * A display EMA smooths the result.
        -:   22: *
        -:   23: * Single-pole EMA replaces the earlier rectangular-window running mean
        -:   24: * for one reason: live biofeedback. A rectangular window holds old
        -:   25: * samples at equal weight until they evict — a step "moving → still"
        -:   26: * stays elevated for a full window-width (~1 s here) before settling,
        -:   27: * which broke the user-perceived feedback loop. An EMA reaches 63 % of
        -:   28: * a step response in one tau and weighs recent samples more, so the
        -:   29: * user sees the metric react in 100-200 ms rather than 1-2 s. The
        -:   30: * trade-off is a noisier output sample-to-sample; the display EMA
        -:   31: * (smoothing_alpha) absorbs that. Note: the per-frame output is a
        -:   32: * weighted RMS, not a rectangular-window RMS — research-grade windowed
        -:   33: * statistics are computed offline from the raw 50 Hz IMU stream that
        -:   34: * the mobile app records per session.
        -:   35: *
        -:   36: * Constants here are starting points; the weights, the decay rate,
        -:   37: * the baselines and the EMA alphas are all exposed through
        -:   38: * @ref stability_config_t for the planned tuning UI.
        -:   39: */
        -:   40:
